        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix referral error message typos and punctuation",
        "summary": "Corrects typos and punctuation in referral redemption error strings within `web/src/app/api/referrals/helpers.ts`. Fixes missing space in 'already.o' to 'already. No' and adds trailing periods to duplicate/self-referral errors. Updates `web/src/app/onboard/page.tsx` to remove redundant period concatenation in UI display logic.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:42:48.947Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you or someone else tries to use a referral code that has already been used, or tries to refer themselves, the error messages will now read more smoothly with proper punctuation and spacing. For example, instead of seeing a confusing message like 'already.o double dipping', you'll see 'already. No double dipping'. These fixes make the error messages clearer and easier to understand when something goes wrong with applying a referral code. The changes are live today.",
